<header class="start-masthead">
<p class="docs-breadcrumb">CyberAlchemy Lab / Guided walkthrough</p>
<h1>Follow an incident</h1>
<p class="start-deck">A customer reports missing records. Follow what an agent needs, what it can establish and how the next decision becomes reviewable.</p>
<p class="start-reading-time">{{READING_TIME}} minute read · The fictional {{CASE_ACCOUNT}} case used throughout the guide</p>
</header>
<section id="report"><h2>1. Start with the customer’s report</h2>
<blockquote class="walk-report"><span>{{CASE_TICKET_ID}} · {{CASE_ACCOUNT}} · Customer support</span><p>“Our customer-data export is missing records. Please investigate the file we received.”</p><footer>Customer-data service owner · Incident open</footer></blockquote>
<p>The report starts a response. It does not yet establish what went wrong. The service owner needs an investigation that can distinguish missing identifiers from an incorrect filter, a changed source or a mistaken expectation.</p>
<ol class="walk-process" aria-label="Investigation sequence">
<li><span>01</span><strong>Define the question</strong><small>Meaning and permission</small></li>
<li><span>02</span><strong>Compare saved inputs</strong><small>Method and observation</small></li>
<li><span>03</span><strong>Assess the omission</strong><small>Evidence and limits</small></li>
<li><span>04</span><strong>Prepare the decision</strong><small>Proposal and owner review</small></li>
</ol>
<p class="figure-note">Read left to right, or top to bottom on a narrow screen. Numbers show the order of this explanation. They do not declare connections between Lab records.</p>
<dl class="walk-step"><div><dt>Agent reads</dt><dd>The customer report and the Incident’s response scope.</dd></div><div><dt>Work to prepare</dt><dd>A bounded investigation within the export-repair Project.</dd></div><div><dt>Needed to proceed</dt><dd>A named owner, an assignment, applicable permission and usable task information.</dd></div></dl>
</section>
<section id="scope"><h2>2. Make the question and boundaries explicit</h2>
<p>The customer-data platform is the <a href="{{DEF:Product}}">Product</a>. Exporting eligible customer data is one of its capabilities. The repair <a href="{{DEF:Project}}">Project</a> coordinates the response; the investigation is a bounded <a href="{{DEF:Work}}">Work</a> item. An <a href="{{DEF:Agent Assignment}}">Agent Assignment</a> identifies the agent’s job.</p>
<figure class="definition-anatomy"><figcaption>Read an accepted definition through four questions</figcaption>
<dl><div><dt>What is the exact meaning?</dt><dd><strong>Complete export · {{CASE_DEFINITION_VERSION}}</strong><br>Every required identifier from the declared account, filters and fixed source snapshot appears in the saved output.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Where does it apply?</dt><dd>Identifier coverage for {{CASE_ACCOUNT}}, <code>{{CASE_FILTERS}}</code>, source snapshot {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}} and saved output {{CASE_OUTPUT}}. Use the same stable identifier on both sides.</dd></div>
<div><dt>What can it establish?</dt><dd><code>RequiredIds({{CASE_SNAPSHOT}}, {{CASE_ACCOUNT}}, F) ⊆ ExportedIds({{CASE_OUTPUT}})</code>. This criterion assesses coverage; it does not assess the accuracy of each value.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Why does it govern here?</dt><dd>The case assumes the responsible owner has accepted this exact definition version for the declared scope. Its acceptance does not grant data access or deployment permission.</dd></div></dl>
</figure>
<p>This is the case’s definition illustration. The <a href="{{DEF:Definition}}">Definition contract</a> additionally requires its exact identity, owner, voices, boundaries and other governed fields; this annotated excerpt helps read those responsibilities.</p>
<dl class="walk-step"><div><dt>Agent reads</dt><dd>The definition, assignment, applicable policies, recorded delegation and checked Context and Ontology Views.</dd></div><div><dt>Scope it records</dt><dd>{{CASE_ACCOUNT}}; <code>{{CASE_FILTERS}}</code>; {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}}; {{CASE_OUTPUT}}; run {{CASE_RUN}}; software revision {{CASE_SERVICE_REVISION}}; completeness definition {{CASE_DEFINITION_VERSION}}.</dd></div><div><dt>Needed to proceed</dt><dd>The separate 30-minute delegation permits inspection, identifier comparison, saving candidate material through the recording route and preparing a proposal.</dd></div></dl>
<p>Changing source data, deploying code, admitting a definition and closing the incident each require their applicable authority. An assignment alone supplies none of those permissions.</p>
</section>
<section id="compare"><h2>3. Compare the selected records</h2>
<p>Use the values in fixed snapshot {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}} to select {{CASE_ACCOUNT}}’s active records. Then compare their stable identifiers with {{CASE_OUTPUT}}. Comparing row counts alone would miss duplicates or a different set of identifiers.</p>
<figure class="coverage-figure"><figcaption>Identifier coverage in the selected export</figcaption>
<div class="coverage-row"><span>Required from {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}}</span><div><strong>{{CASE_REQUIRED_COUNT}}</strong><span class="coverage-track" aria-hidden="true"><i style="width:100%"></i></span></div></div>
<div class="coverage-row"><span>Present in {{CASE_OUTPUT}}</span><div><strong>{{CASE_OUTPUT_ROW_COUNT}}</strong><span class="coverage-track" aria-hidden="true"><i style="width:98%"></i></span></div></div>
<p><strong>Missing required identifiers: {{CASE_MISSING_COUNT}}.</strong> The case’s required identifiers are 1–{{CASE_REQUIRED_COUNT}}; {{CASE_OUTPUT}} contains 1–{{CASE_OUTPUT_ROW_COUNT}}.</p></figure>
<dl class="walk-step"><div><dt>Agent reads</dt><dd>The saved source and output, the selection rule and comparison method version {{CASE_METHOD_VERSION}}.</dd></div><div><dt>Agent produces</dt><dd>An <a href="{{DEF:Operational Observation}}">Operational Observation</a> of the missing identifiers, with attributable inputs, method and result.</dd></div><div><dt>Needed to proceed</dt><dd>Save the material through the permitted recording route, retaining its exact sources and limitations.</dd></div></dl>
<p>The observation records what happened. The method, selected data and result make it examinable. A new snapshot or changed filter would need its own comparison.</p>
</section>
<section id="evidence"><h2>4. Connect the result to a bounded assessment</h2>
<p>The agent assembles an <a href="{{DEF:Evidence Set}}">Evidence Set</a> for the omission claim. A <a href="{{DEF:Failure Assessment}}">Failure Assessment</a> evaluates the occurrence, mode, cause, impact, containment, recovery and uncertainty independently.</p>
<figure class="record-trail"><figcaption>Three declared connection signatures used by this case</figcaption>
<div class="relation-reading"><strong>Operational Observation</strong><span class="relation-arrow">originates-from <span class="direction-right" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="direction-down" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><small>origin role: required-input</small></span><strong>Source {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}}</strong></div>
<div class="relation-reading"><strong>Operational Observation</strong><span class="relation-arrow">originates-from <span class="direction-right" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="direction-down" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><small>origin role: observed-output</small></span><strong>Source {{CASE_OUTPUT}}</strong></div>
<div class="relation-reading"><strong>Evidence Set</strong><span class="relation-arrow">evidence-bears-on <span class="direction-right" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="direction-down" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><small>polarity: supports</small></span><strong>Failure Assessment</strong></div>
<p class="figure-note">Arrows name actual permitted ordered kind pairs. A saved connection must also satisfy its full contract, including exact endpoint references. These signatures are not complete validated instances.</p></figure>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="learning-table"><caption>What the comparison establishes</caption><thead><tr><th>Assessment question</th><th>Current conclusion</th><th>Next evidence needed</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>Did omission occur?</th><td>{{CASE_MISSING_COUNT}} required identifiers are absent from {{CASE_OUTPUT}}.</td><td>The saved inputs, method and comparison support this scoped result.</td></tr>
<tr><th>What caused it?</th><td>Unresolved.</td><td>Investigate how the selected input became this output.</td></tr>
<tr><th>How far does it reach?</th><td>Confirmed in {{CASE_OUTPUT}}; wider impact unresolved.</td><td>Inspect other outputs and downstream uses within authorized scope.</td></tr>
<tr><th>Has recovery succeeded?</th><td>Unestablished.</td><td>Assess the recovery result against its declared criteria.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<dl class="walk-step"><div><dt>Agent reads</dt><dd>The source-bound observation and the requirements for the claim being assessed.</dd></div><div><dt>Agent produces</dt><dd>Candidate assessment material with the omission established and other postures left unresolved.</dd></div><div><dt>Needed to proceed</dt><dd>Review evidence for the particular conclusion and record its standing. Evidence presence alone does not accept a claim or decide a response.</dd></div></dl>
</section>
<section id="proposal"><h2>5. Prepare a repair proposal for a decision</h2>
<p>The case includes proposed software revision {{CASE_FIX_REVISION}}. Its repair effect has not been established. A useful proposal identifies what would change, the suspected mechanism, how to assess it, the affected scope and unresolved questions.</p>
<dl class="walk-step"><div><dt>Agent reads</dt><dd>The implementation’s recorded identity and version, scoped assessment and applicable constraints.</dd></div><div><dt>Agent prepares</dt><dd>A candidate change proposal and a plan for checking identifier coverage and other required behavior.</dd></div><div><dt>Needed for a later transition</dt><dd>The responsible owner reviews the exact revision, evidence and requested effects. Adoption, activation, recovery and closure retain their own requirements.</dd></div></dl>
<figure class="review-route"><figcaption>A possible later route, after sufficient evidence and authority</figcaption>
<ol><li><strong>Assess the proposed revision</strong><span>Collect evidence for the repair claim and relevant constraints.</span></li><li><strong>Record the owner’s decision</strong><span>Identify the exact change and effects approved, if any.</span></li><li><strong>Perform the permitted change</strong><span>Record the authorized write, release or deployment through its applicable route.</span></li><li><strong>Assess recovery and closure</strong><span>Establish the response criteria before the owner changes the incident’s closure state.</span></li></ol>
<p class="figure-note">This is a conditional process illustration. The {{CASE_ACCOUNT}} case stops before these results are established.</p></figure>
<p><a href="../craft-documentation-proposal/craft-model.html#governance">Craft can help express and construct the software change.</a> Generated code and checks can become Work outputs. Their existence does not admit Lab records or authorize deployment.</p>
</section>
<section id="handoff"><h2>6. Resume from saved knowledge in a new session</h2>
<p>At 10:10, task view {{CASE_VIEW_VERSION}} has expired. The agent pauses because it cannot rely on that view for the next action. This does not mean its 30-minute delegation has necessarily expired; view usability and permission have separate conditions.</p>
<figure class="session-handoff"><figcaption>Continuity across temporary agent sessions</figcaption>
<ol><li data-model-concept="agent">{{AGENT_ICON}}<div><strong>Session {{CASE_SESSION}}</strong><span>Persist permitted observations, evidence, candidate material and the handoff before terminating. Short-term Session Memory ends with the session.</span></div></li>
<li data-model-concept="project">{{PROJECT_STATE_ICON}}<div><strong>Durable Project State</strong><span>Saved records keep their exact versions, provenance, standing, decisions and unresolved matters. Saving a proposal does not accept it.</span></div></li>
<li data-model-concept="agent">{{AGENT_ICON}}<div><strong>A later session</strong><span>A new machine-agent instance receives an assignment, separately checked permission and fresh Context and Ontology Views selected from saved state.</span></div></li></ol>
<p class="figure-note">Read top to bottom: permitted writes preserve knowledge; newly checked views select it for later work. No session memory or authority is transferred by this diagram.</p></figure>
<p>The next agent can recover the {{CASE_MISSING_COUNT}}-identifier omission and the candidate proposal. It still needs to investigate cause, establish wider impact and assess any recovery. Continuity preserves both knowledge and its limits.</p>
<nav class="start-reading-paths" aria-label="Continue from the walkthrough"><a href="concept-comparisons.html"><strong>Compare the concepts</strong><span>Revisit observation, evidence, assessment, work and agent views.</span></a><a href="governance-lab-reference.html#learning"><strong>Continue into operational learning</strong><span>Turn experience into a scoped lesson, then assess later use and benefit.</span></a><a href="lab-reference-library.html#catalog-types"><strong>Inspect the record contracts</strong><span>Find the full fields and constraints behind the illustrated records.</span></a></nav>
</section>
